completed_at: "2026-10-31T02:24:35.947Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Reproduce a ready P0 population competing with automated P2 comment churn;Define explicit default and caller-customizable ranking policy;Verify explanations and SDK CLI MCP parity with bounded token costs
parent: pm-4k6b
risk: medium
confidence: 60
resolution: "NextOptions.rankingPolicy and the context.next_ranking_policy setting select priority_floor (default: in-progress work first, then priority tiers, relevance within a tier, applied only to the built-in weighted model) or weighted (blended order). filters.ranking_policy discloses the policy on every transport, recommendation reasons name a policy/score disagreement, unknown policies refuse as invalid_argument_value, and docs/COMMANDS.md, docs/CONFIGURATION.md and docs/SDK.md describe the contract."
expected_result: Default next-work advice cannot silently elevate an automated P2 log above ready P0 work; documented policy and ranking explanations match tested behavior.
actual_result: "Isolated tracker: a P2 log with 12 comments beside a P1 and a P0 is ranked [P0, P1, log] under the default and the weighted policy follows the score order while naming the passed-over priority; in-progress work still resumes first; the setting and the SDK override both drive filters.ranking_policy. Real tracker: the floor moves a churned P2 chore (baseline rank 38) below every P1. Negative control: with next.ts stashed the new tests fail. Agent-task token baseline raised by the 10-token filters field; all other gates unchanged and green."
