comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T16:11:10.969Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete initial strict3146-item all-status corpus plus fresh specific searches and open/in-progress inventories found no existing owner for GH1618. Read full live pm-4k6b and completed pm-1mwk/pm-07pt16 lineage. This new report arrived during PR1619 validation and remains open/unclaimed; no reproduction or fix is asserted."
  "2026-10-31T02:23:26.465Z","harness:claude-code","Reproduced on current source. The default scorer (default-weighted-v1) blends ten signals; priority_pressure carries about 11% of the normalizing weight while recency, activity_density and knowledge_density (all raised by comment_add events, which event classification treats as substantive regardless of author) carry about 27%, so a P2 item with steady comment churn can outscore ready P0/P1 work. There is no automation marker on comments or history (author_source/agent_harness only), and no settings key influenced the order. Real-tracker evidence (229 open, 112 ready, pm next --limit 5 --explain-ranking): under the blended order a P2 chore with activity_density 0.233 and recency 0.294 (baseline rank 38) ranks 5th above P1 items; under the new default priority floor it drops below every P1 and rank 5 becomes a P1 (baseline 20). An isolated-tracker test seeds a P2 log with 12 comments beside a P1 and a P0: the floor recommends the P0 and ranks [P0, P1, log]; the weighted policy follows the score order and names the passed-over priority in reasons when the log wins."
  "2026-10-31T02:23:26.971Z","harness:claude-code","Fix: NextOptions.rankingPolicy and the context.next_ranking_policy setting (pm config project set context_next_ranking_policy weighted) select priority_floor (default) or weighted. priority_floor reorders only the built-in weighted model's output: in-progress work first (the documented resume contract), then priority tiers, relevance order inside a tier; an extension context_relevance scorer keeps its own order under either policy. filters.ranking_policy discloses the policy on CLI, SDK and MCP; the recommendation reasons add 'priority floor (relevance rank N)' or 'relevance over pN ready work' when policy and score disagree; --explain-ranking keeps each item's score beside its final rank. An unknown policy refuses as invalid_argument_value listing the accepted values. The agent-task token baseline moved by the 10 tokens the new filters field costs on the next step (722 to 732); token-budget, context-intent calibration, refusal-closure, docs-skills, static quality, contracts and capability-surface checks pass; the SDK surface snapshot acknowledges the new option, receipt field, exports and setting."
